eria It is considered to be a delicacy among some Nigerians, and is sometimes served during occasions of importance. Edikang ikong is a nutritious soup and expensive to prepare, and has been described as being mostly eaten by rich people in Nigeria. Ingredients used in edikang ikong include beef and dried fish, bush meat, crayfish, shaki (cow tripe), kanda, pumpkin leaves, water leaves, ikong ubong, onion, periwinkle, palm oil, salt and pepper."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-edikang-ikong"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edikang_ikong"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Nigerian cuisine","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Catharanthus roseus","ingredient/catharanthus-roseus"],["Crayfish","ingredient/crayfish"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Palm oil","ingredient/palm-oil"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Waterleaf","ingredient/waterleaf"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kitchen Butterfly","ref":"site/kitchenbutterfly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenbutterfly.com","note":"Long-running blog by Nigerian food writer and historian Ozoz Sokoh, with Nigerian and New Nigerian recipes.","url":"https://www.kitchenbutterfly.com/about-2","suggested":true},{"name":"Sisi Yemmie","ref":"site/sisiyemmie-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sisiyemmie.com","note":"Nigerian home cooking recipes and meal plans, paired with the SisiYemmieTV YouTube channel.","url":"https://sisiyemmie.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Nigerian cuisine","links":[["Akadi","dish/akadi"],["Edo black soup","dish/edo-black-soup"],["Miyar zogale","dish/miyar-zogale"],["Moin moin","dish/moin-moin"],["Ofada rice","dish/ofada-rice"],["Palm nut soup","dish/palm-nut-soup"],["Sinasir","dish/sinasir"],["Suya","dish/suya"]]}]},"dish/franks-diner":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/franks-diner","n":"Franks Diner","c":"#ede6da","cr