an","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}]},"dish/prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau","n":"Prawn cocktail, steak and Black Forest gateau","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Prawn cocktail, steak garni with chips, and Black Forest gâteau was the most popular dinner menu in British restaurants in the 1980s, according to contemporary surveys by trade magazine Caterer and Hotelkeeper. It was associated with the Berni Inn chain, which popularised mass-market dining out after the end of food rationing in Britain following the Second World War. The Prawn Cocktail Years, by Simon Hopkinson and Lindsey Bareham, called this meal the Great British Meal Out."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prawn_cocktail%2C_steak_and_Black_Forest_gateau"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chefs: traditional British recipes","ref":"site/greatbritishchefs-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatbritishchefs.com","note":"UK chef-driven recipe site with a large section of classic British dishes.","url":"https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/features/our-most-popular-traditional-british-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from British cuisine","links":[["68–86 Bar and Restaurant","dish/68-86-bar-and-restaurant"],["Banbury cake","dish/banbury-cake"],["Battenberg cake","dish/battenberg-cake"],["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"],["Bread sauce","dish/bread-sauce"],["Carpetbag steak","dish/carpetbag-steak"],["Chelsea bun","dish/chelsea-bun"],["Christmas pudding","dish/christmas-pudding"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Crumble","dish/crumble"],["Crumpet","dish/crumpet"],["Curry in the United Kingdom","dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom"],["Digestive biscuit","dish/digestive-biscuit"],["Dinner by Heston Blumenthal","dish/dinner-by-heston-blumenthal"],["Dundee cake","dish/dundee-cake"],["English muffin","dish/english-muffin"],["Flies' graveyard","dish/flies-graveyard"],["Flummery","dish/flummery"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"],["Garibaldi biscuit","dish/garibaldi-biscuit"],["Gidleigh Park","dish/gidleigh-park"],["Hot cross bun","dish/hot-cross-bun"],["Hovis biscuit","dish/hovis-biscuit"],["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"],["Melba toast","dish/melba-toast"],["Mince pie","dish/mince-pie"],["Phall","dish/phall"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Ploughman's lunch","dish/ploughman-s-lunch"],["Potted shrimps","dish/potted-shrimps"],["Restaurant Andrew Fairlie","dish/restaurant-andrew-fairlie"],["Restaurant James Sommerin","dish/restaurant-james-sommerin"],["Rhodes Twenty Four","dish/rhodes-twenty-four"],["Rich tea","dish/rich-tea"],["Rose & Crown Pub & Dining Room","dish/rose-crown-pub-dining-room"],["Sausage roll","dish/sausage-roll"],["Scotch egg","dish/scotch-egg"],["Shepherd's pie","dish/shepherd-s-pie"],["Soldiers (food)","dish/soldiers-food"]]}]},"dish/semla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/semla","n":"Semla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A semla, laskiaispulla, Swedish eclair, fastlagsbulle,  fastelavnsbolle, vastlakukkel, or vēja kūkas is a traditional sweet roll made in various forms in Sweden, Finland, Estonia, Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Iceland, Norway, and Latvia, associated with Lent and especially Shrove Tuesday in most countries, Shrove Monday in Denmark, parts of southern Sweden, Iceland and Faroe Islands or Sunday of Fastelavn in Norway. In Sweden it is most commonly known as just semla, but is also known as fettisdagsbulle, lit. 'Fat Tuesday bun' or 'Shrove Tuesday bun'. In the southern parts of Sweden, as well as in Swedish-speaking Finland, it is known as fastlagsbulle (plural: fastlagsbullar; semla on the other hand means a plain wheat bun with butter, called bulle in Swedish). In Poland it is known as ptyś. In Estonia it is called vastlakukkel. In Norway and Denmark it is called fastelavn"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-semla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine"],["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Almond paste","ingredient/almond-paste"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Wheat bread","ingredient/wheat-bread"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scandicuisine: Swedish recipes","ref":"site/scandicuisine-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scandicuisine.com","note":"Traditional Swedish recipes from Cecilia, a cook from a Finnish-Swedish family on Åland.","url":"https://scandicuisine.com/category/swedish-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Finnish cuisine","links":[["Blodpalt","dish/blodpalt"],["Cabbage rol